# VAV System Model

This VAV model is designed for your existing `SystemSimulationProvider`.

It matches the simulator's current VAV point set:

- Zone-Temp
- Cooling-SP
- Heating-SP
- Damper-Cmd
- Zone-Airflow
- Reheat-Valve
- Occupancy
- Zone-CO2

Recommended mapping:

```text
MODEL INPUT                 SIMULATOR POINT

cooling_setpoint_c      <-  VAV / Cooling-SP
heating_setpoint_c      <-  VAV / Heating-SP
occupied                <-  VAV / Occupancy
supply_air_temp_c       <-  Serving AHU / SAT

MODEL OUTPUT                SIMULATOR POINT

zone_temp_c             ->  VAV / Zone-Temp
damper_command_pct      ->  VAV / Damper-Cmd
zone_airflow_cfm        ->  VAV / Zone-Airflow
reheat_valve_pct        ->  VAV / Reheat-Valve
zone_co2_ppm            ->  VAV / Zone-CO2
```

No separate participant UI is needed. Mapping `supply_air_temp_c` to the serving
AHU's SAT automatically makes that AHU part of the model context internally.

Suggested "Add Model" parameters:

- Minimum Airflow
- Maximum Airflow
- Zone Thermal Response
- Cooling Proportional Band
- Heating Proportional Band
- Max Reheat Temperature Rise
- Outdoor CO2

Behavior:
- cooling demand opens damper and raises airflow
- heating demand holds minimum airflow and opens reheat
- zone temperature reacts to supply air plus internal load
- CO2 rises with occupancy and falls with ventilation
